{"route":"/docs/5.0/helpers/visually-hidden/","version":"5.0","renderedVersion":"5.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Visually hidden","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use these helpers to visually hide elements but keep them accessible to assistive technologies."},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Visually hide an element while still allowing it to be exposed to assistive technologies (such as screen readers) with <code>.visually-hidden</code>. Use <code>.visually-hidden-focusable</code> to visually hide an element by default, but to display it when it’s focused (e.g. by a keyboard-only user). <code>.visually-hidden-focusable</code> can also be applied to a container–thanks to <code>:focus-within</code>, the container will be displayed when any child element of the container receives focus."},{"id":"content--example-1","type":"demo","key":"dcc9fe00314e497b2d65","height":201},{"id":"content--code-1","type":"code","value":"<h2 class=\"visually-hidden\">Title for screen readers</h2>\n<a class=\"visually-hidden-focusable\" href=\"#content\">Skip to main content</a>\n<div class=\"visually-hidden-focusable\">A container with a <a href=\"#\">focusable element</a>.</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"content--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Both <code>visually-hidden</code> and <code>visually-hidden-focusable</code> can also be used as mixins."},{"id":"content--code-2","type":"code","value":"// Usage as a mixin\n\n.visually-hidden-title {\n  @include visually-hidden;\n}\n\n.skip-navigation {\n  @include visually-hidden-focusable;\n}","language":"scss"}],"demos":[{"key":"dcc9fe00314e497b2d65","html":"\n<h2 class=\"visually-hidden\">Title for screen readers</h2>\n<a class=\"visually-hidden-focusable\" href=\"#content\">Skip to main content</a>\n<div class=\"visually-hidden-focusable\">A container with a <a href=\"#\">focusable element</a>.</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":"